<Layout title="Owner Setup Guide | Home is Cookie" description="Owner instructions for Cloudflare, Jotform and Square, Kit, Search Console, Analytics, Bing, and honest review requests."><article class="wrap prose"><p class="eyebrow">Owner setup · After design approval</p><h1>The connections<br/><em>behind your website.</em></h1><p>This page is a setup guide. No payment, email campaign, DNS record, or analytics account has been changed by building the prototype.</p><h2>1. Cloudflare Pages</h2><p>Cloudflare remains the hosting fit for this static site and your existing account. Hosting location alone does not improve search rankings; rendered content, reliable performance, accurate business information, and crawl access matter.</p><ol><li>Keep Home is Cookie in its own project, separate from taittfin.net.</li><li>For the Astro source, use <code>npm run build</code> and output directory <code>dist</code>. The earlier <code>exit 0</code> / root-directory settings were for the original plain HTML site.</li><li>For direct upload, upload the compiled static package contents with index.html at the root.</li><li>Keep previews private/noindex. Set <code>PUBLIC_SITE_LAUNCH=true</code> only for the approved production build.</li><li>Connect www.homeiscookie.com in Pages, verify its Active status, configure the apex redirect, and remove the old Canva redirect where it is actually managed. Preserve email DNS records.</li><li>Check robots.txt and Cloudflare WAF / bot settings for OAI-SearchBot access. Preserve existing GPTBot preferences separately.</li></ol><h2>2. Jotform + Square: a paper trail</h2><p>Use the existing hosted form for the prototype. Update a duplicate test form later so the live form is not silently changed.</p><ol><li>Reconcile products, prices, minimums, cake sizes/servings, notice, artwork, and delivery fields against the approved public catalog.</li><li>Collect the request first. Review capacity, date, artwork, delivery fee, tax where applicable, and the final total.</li><li>Send an itemized approved quote with one stable order reference, quote version, remaining-balance deadline, and terms.</li><li>After approval, offer a 50% non-refundable deposit or full payment. Bind the approved amount using a trusted provider configuration. A browser-editable price or URL parameter cannot authorize a charge.</li><li>Confirm captured Square payment status and exact amount. A thank-you page or PDF alone does not prove payment.</li><li>Retain the request, approved quote, accepted terms, payment receipt, balance, and fulfillment record under the same order reference. Reconcile duplicate notifications and payment failures.</li></ol><p>If the tested Jotform setup cannot enforce the deposit and balance workflow, review Square Invoices as a fallback before changing the customer experience. No deposit automation is claimed in this prototype.</p><h2>3. Kit signup and welcome sequence</h2><p>The newsletter button opens your existing Kit signup page. Confirm the signup, consent wording, confirmation email, unsubscribe, and plan capabilities before enabling a sequence. Marketing consent stays separate from ordering.</p><ul><li><strong>After confirmed signup:</strong> “Welcome to Home is Cookie.” Introduce LaTasha and her grandmother’s recipe. Link to the cookie menu.</li><li><strong>Two days later:</strong> “Something for your next get-together.” Introduce the $50 sharing tray and stuffed cookies. Link to ordering.</li><li><strong>Five days after signup:</strong> “A thank-you with your name on it.” Introduce corporate boxes and printed cookies. Use local delivery content for Sun City Center-only interests where supported.</li></ul><p>Complete email copy, consent rules, and the reconciliation design are included in the downloadable source package under <code>docs/SETUP-GUIDE.md</code>.</p><h2>4. Google Search Console</h2><ol><li>Open <a href="https://search.google.com/search-console/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Search Console</a> with the business owner’s Google account.</li><li>Add a Domain property for <code>homeiscookie.com</code>.</li><li>Copy the exact TXT verification record Google provides into Cloudflare DNS. Keep existing records.</li><li>Verify the property, then submit <code>https://www.homeiscookie.com/sitemap.xml</code> after launch.</li><li>Inspect the homepage, corporate-gifts page, and Sun City Center page. Confirm their live canonical and indexability, then request indexing where appropriate.</li></ol><h2>5. Google Analytics</h2><ol><li>Open <a href="https://analytics.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics</a> and create a GA4 property for Home is Cookie, with the business timezone and USD currency.</li><li>Create a Web data stream for the final HTTPS website. Record its G- measurement ID.</li><li>Choose the appropriate privacy/consent setup, add the official tag once, and verify with DebugView / Realtime.</li><li>Record order clicks and corporate quote clicks as intent. Only confirmed provider submissions are leads; only reconciled captured payments are payments.</li><li>Keep deposits, remaining balances, and full-order revenue distinct. Never double-count a deposit and a full total as two purchases.</li></ol><h2>6. Bing Webmaster Tools</h2><ol><li>Open <a href="https://www.bing.com/webmasters/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bing Webmaster Tools</a> in an owner-controlled account.</li><li>Import the verified Search Console property, or add and verify the site using the displayed method.</li><li>Confirm the sitemap and inspect priority URLs. Monitor crawling and available performance reports.</li></ol><h2>7. Reviews and customer photos</h2><p>The private preview shows a real excerpt from the Facebook comment screenshot you supplied. Confirm its original link and permission before public use. Google reviews must be supplied or retrieved accurately before display; Facebook reviews cannot be moved into Google as customer-authored reviews.</p><ol><li>In the verified Google Business Profile, open the review-request sharing option and copy the direct review link.</li><li>Request an honest review 24–48 hours after confirmed fulfillment. Apply the request consistently; no incentive and no screening for only happy customers.</li><li>Suggested wording: “Thank you for ordering from Home is Cookie. If you have a moment, would you share an honest Google review of your experience? Your feedback helps other local customers find us.”</li><li>Add a verified review QR code to packaging once the link is tested.</li><li>Approve customer photo rights and marketing consent separately. Keep submissions private until reviewed.</li></ol><p>Update <code>src/data/reviews.js</code> with verified excerpts and source links. The strip becomes scrollable when multiple approved entries exist; it pauses on hover/focus and supports reduced motion.</p><h2>8. Launch checks</h2><p>Resolve the menu and policy questions in the owner review page. Test representative orders, deposits, full payments, failures, receipts, and signup confirmation using supported test modes. Then verify the public domain’s photos, social preview, metadata, redirects, crawl rules, and mobile order path.</p><a class="button" href="/prototype-notes/">Back to open items →</a></article></Layout>
